target_id":"1f9c-b3a8-33e1-43bb"},{"link_uuid":"3a8a40f8-2045-4758-b06a-ada1d72054cd","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"bc4e-d6f7-87a7-436a"},{"link_uuid":"9a0961f6-9b23-4a82-9856-fe35c81b3d59","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"528d-185c-b1ea-4767"},{"link_uuid":"63041913-cc18-410d-995d-7cf56e71cfba","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"50a1-c968-b034-4071"},{"link_uuid":"bfe3a48d-0603-4b01-9e12-a08c69962f66","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"0a00-6722-48ed-4a2f"},{"link_uuid":"d5ada309-bab0-4e05-87a7-e5d6195269c8","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"c4e1-abfd-ddb7-4b67"},{"link_uuid":"130f248d-fb7e-430a-8d7d-84406ebd3d75","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"28bc-c8f0-f638-4b94"},{"link_uuid":"404f9caa-fdfb-49cd-a32f-0e5a0761ffa8","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"c9c7-49bf-e717-4419"},{"link_uuid":"bce49ed4-e72d-4c65-b7c3-e9dae024f522","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"2b50-6568-988e-485d"},{"link_uuid":"85bf43ed-9c1b-4f8f-908a-ccd8329126fd","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"79a6-6533-b7b5-4dd4"},{"link_uuid":"49cfc330-b1b6-49ce-bbdc-e671046d4c15","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"2172-3078-6e9d-404e"},{"link_uuid":"820502d2-f442-4f89-a06a-06753148f212","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"835c-a544-6577-4c69"},{"link_uuid":"3b59fab9-0578-4883-a9d5-a63856559ff7","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"fdc8-ae18-e190-4db6"},{"link_uuid":"c4be7c45-3012-4382-8440-1c47c21b35b8","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"78d5-5e5d-1e9f-432f"},{"link_uuid":"a3b4cd16-985a-4993-9f8d-5b41907b1e0f","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"a767-282a-7ca1-4ae2"},{"link_uuid":"2ff80db4-c1e4-4b0b-abc1-3037fcf2e5c1","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"7e36-5d52-878f-4adc"},{"link_uuid":"c945e003-f199-4121-9139-7f3fa19743b5","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"62ac-ace9-2c0e-4668"},{"link_uuid":"928c5db5-6fa6-4bbe-a198-bf603a736ef5","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"c471-5ef2-f39b-4e64"}],"description":"## Context / Problem\nThe tests/scripts cohort contains audited comments or docstrings that obscure current behavior with repetition, obvious narration, duplicated explanation, or historical detail. The audit is pinned to `9e65567b79ffe872534c3c656ade7b34340d8192`.\n\n## Approach\nEdit explanatory text only in this directory/subsystem cohort. Condense it to current, non-obvious rationale and constraints; retain every file-specific preserve item and consumer contract below. Grouping adjacent files from one subsystem keeps the change reviewable in one session and permits one coherent verification pass without changing executable behavior.\n\n## Scope\n- `tests/scripts/conftest.py:1-6, 32-35, 74-81, 111-131` — Preserve import-path necessity, capture contract, and network isolation. Consumer: none found.\n- `tests/scripts/test_alert_dedup.py:1-12, 95-102` — Preserve lane-specific marker namespaces and string timestamp acceptance. Consumer: none found.\n- `tests/scripts/test_autodeploy_disk_pressure.py:1-16, 291-293, 405-460` — Preserve quiescent-tick reclaim, measured before/after logging, persistence-only alerting, and distinct marker tokens. Consumer: none found.\n- `tests/scripts/test_autodeploy_fetch_secrets.py:1-17` — Preserve secret refresh-before-compose ordering and failure stop. Consumer: none found.\n- `tests/scripts/test_autodeploy_health_gate.py:1-15, 170-175, 246-255` — Preserve deadline-above-app budget, pre-rollback stderr capture, and marker-injection protection. Consumer: none found.\n- `tests/scripts/test_autodeploy_materialize_certbot.py:1-16` — Preserve installer-source trigger and host timer materialization. Consumer: none found.\n- `tests/scripts/test_autodeploy_materialize_probe.py:1-14` — Preserve observability source-to-host-copy trigger. Consumer: none found.\n- `tests/scripts/test_autodeploy_mcp_bluegreen.py:1-18, 510-521, 650-658, 692-698, 1622-1672, 1700-1764, 1997-2004, 2144-2153, 2333-2341, 2477-2490` — Preserve atomic cutover, component-scoped backoff/accounting, safe image retention, handshake/store readiness, and unconditional live-backend protection. Consumer: none found.\n- `tests/scripts/test_autodeploy_review_drain.py:1-20, 296-301, 346-353, 443-464, 489-501, 637-712` — Preserve busy/mid-redeploy deferral, bounded episode semantics, signal-unavailable fail-open behavior, and observability markers. Consumer: none found.\n- `tests/scripts/test_autodeploy_signals_gerrit_config.py:1-24, 41-44` — Preserve detect-only/manual-apply classification and operator-facing detail. Consumer: none found.\n- `tests/scripts/test_autodeploy_signals_nginx_edge.py:1-22, 62-64` — Preserve detect-only manual apply for the edge template. Consumer: none found.\n- `tests/scripts/test_autodeploy_signals_nginx_materializer.py:1-29` — Preserve materializer-source detection and manual-apply classification. Consumer: none found.\n- `tests/scripts/test_binding_lifecycle_grace_seam_clean_heldout.py:1-29, 116-119` — Preserve zero below-seam reads and live grace wiring. Consumer: none found.\n- `tests/scripts/test_canary_bridge.py:1-30` — Preserve immediate drift alerting versus thresholded heartbeat alerting. Consumer: none found.\n- `tests/scripts/test_check_adr_numbers.py:1-27` — Preserve ADR/marker bijection and duplicate-number detection. Consumer: none found.\n- `tests/scripts/test_check_config_ownership_heldout.py:1-12, 44-46, 84-86, 130-132, 150-152, 177-179, 189-191, 203-205, 246-248` — Preserve adversarial detection shapes and real-tree cleanliness. Consumer: none found.\n- `tests/scripts/test_check_config_ownership.py:1-19` — Preserve approved ownership seams and fail-closed classification. Consumer: none found.\n- `tests/scripts/test_check_config_reads_heldout.py:110-119, 243-247, 272-277, 322-333` — Preserve negative string-read fixtures and closed-ticket marker reporting. Consumer: none found.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Every listed location contains only current, non-obvious rationale or constraints after remediation; verified by reviewing the final diff against every 